// What the backdoor could actually do, once activated.
// Exercises: markdown + animated `scale` AND animated `angle` on the
// key glyph — the two animation features that previously had no
// worked-example slot. Also non-default scroll_speed for pacing.
{
  title: "What it enabled",
  scroll_range: 1200,
  scroll_speed: 0.7,
  // Snap on the animation keyframes: key opaque @400, key upright @600,
  // footnote revealed @900, plus start/end.
  snap_positions: [0, 400, 600, 900, 1200],
  elements: [
    {
      name: "caption",
      markdown: "## Auth bypass + RCE\n\nThe backdoor checked every incoming SSH connection's certificate signature against an attacker-controlled **Ed448 public key**. A match would skip authentication and pass the payload to a code-execution sink.",
      position: [8, 15], anchor: [0, 0],
      width: 55, height: "auto",
      color: "#5a2c2c",
    },
    // The key glyph — animated scale + animated angle as scroll
    // progresses (zooms in and rotates).
    {
      name: "key",
      image: "../key-glyph.svg",
      position: [80, 55], anchor: [50, 50],
      width: 20, height: "auto",
      scale: { keyframes: [[0, 0.5], [600, 1.0], [1200, 1.4]] },
      angle: { keyframes: [[0, -30], [600, 0], [1200, 25]] },
      opacity: { keyframes: [[0, 0.3], [400, 1]] },
    },
    {
      name: "footnote",
      markdown: "*Only the holder of the matching Ed448 private key could trigger the bypass — i.e. the attackers themselves.*",
      position: [8, 75], anchor: [0, 0],
      width: 55, height: "auto",
      color: "#7a4c4c",
      opacity: { keyframes: [[600, 0], [900, 1]] },
    },
  ],
}
